  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only config (config_005: scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) achieves 0.650 acc, while the only multimodal test (config_030: same RNA setup + resnet50 + concat fusion) achieves 0.632, slightly underperforming the unimodal baseline. This raises the question of whether concat fusion is the bottleneck or whether the image modality itself is unhelpful. Question tested: config_031 changes only the fusion method (concat → weighted) while keeping all other settings identical to config_030, providing a controlled test of whether the fusion strategy explains the multimodal underperformance. Why best next experiment: It is the most informative single-variable experiment available. If weighted fusion recovers or exceeds 0.650, we identify fusion strategy as a critical design lever and have a promising multimodal direction to exploit. If it also underperforms, we can rule out fusion as the issue and redirect budget toward testing a stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) or confirming that RNA-only is the superior architecture. Either outcome sharply reduces uncertainty about the most important remaining design decision (whether and how to combine modalities) under a tight budget."
}

